<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Elizabeth, New Jersey</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Elizabethtown</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Elizabeth is a city in north-eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-jersey">New Jersey</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a>, founded in 1664 as Elizabethtown, the first English settlement in the colony. Named after Elizabeth Carteret, wife of the proprietor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/george-carteret">Sir George Carteret</a>, it was the first capital of New Jersey and of East Jersey. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/princeton-university">College of New Jersey</a>, later Princeton University, held its first classes there in 1747.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/elizabeth-new-jersey.jpg" alt="Elizabeth, New Jersey" width="320" height="179" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Quintin Soloviev · CC BY 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Skyline_of_Elizabeth,_New_Jersey_(cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
